allowed), no '#EXT-X-MAP:' \u2192 passes. Good.\n\nWait \u2014 careful with the regex: '#EXT-X-KEY:METHOD=(?!NONE|AES-128)' \u2014 for the line '#EXT-X-KEY:METHOD=NONE', after 'METHOD=' the lookahead (?!NONE|AES-128) fails since 'NONE' follows \u2192 no match. Good.\n\nHmm, one more: '#EXTINF:10,' lines start with '#' \u2192 comment branch. Good.\n\nNow \u2014 the counting loop counts media_frags: seg0, seg1 \u2192 2. Good.\n\n### Also \u2014 should I verify `ctx` contents passed to prepare? calls['prepare'][0] includes 'filename': 'out.ts', 'total_frags': 2, 'ad_frags': 0. I assert total_frags/ad_frags. Good.\n\n### Now, one concern about `patch_fragment_methods` and `dict(ctx)` in fake_prepare: ctx at that point has filename, total_frags, ad_frags. dict(ctx) copies. Good.\n\n### Another concern: in test 10, the HTTPError instance is reused for multiple raises \u2014 fine (exceptions can be raised multiple times).\n\n### Let me also think about whether `dl.real_download` could raise due to `self.to_screen` \u2014 FileDownloader.to_screen \u2192 ydl.to_screen \u2014 quiet \u2192 no-op. Good.\n\n### What about `report_progress` hook added in __init__ \u2014 `self.add_progress_hook(self.report_progress)` \u2014 just appends to list. Good.\n\n### Now write the final file. Also include a brief module docstring. Keep top-level code to imports + helper defs + test functions. No pytest.main.\n\nLet me also reconsider: should `make_downloader` use `monkeypatch.setattr(ydl, 'urlopen', ...)`? ydl is created inside the helper \u2014 monkeypatch fixture is passed in. Fine.\n\nOne more potential issue: `YoutubeDL` may emit warnings on init? No.\n\nAlso \u2014 `from youtube_dl.downloader import hls as hls_module` \u2014 importing hls imports FFmpegFD (external module) and Crypto. Should be fine in the test environment.\n\nLet me also double-check `compat_struct_pack` is importable from youtube_dl.compat \u2014 the snippet itself imports it from there. Good.\n\nNow, about assertion in test 14: `aes_calls[0].iv == compat_struct_pack('>8xq', 5)` \u2014 media_sequence at the time of seg0 download: MEDIA-SEQUENCE:5 set media_sequence=5; no increments before seg0. So iv = pack('>8xq', 5) = b'\\x00'*8 + b'\\x00\\x00\\x00\\x00\\x00\\x00\\x00\\x05'. Good.\n\nWait \u2014 order of lines: '#EXT-X-MEDIA-SEQUENCE:5' comes before the KEY line and fragment. In the download loop, lines processed in order: MEDIA-SEQUENCE \u2192 media_sequence=5; EXT-X-KEY \u2192 decrypt_info set; seg0 \u2192 frag download, iv computed with media_sequence=5. Good.\n\n### Test 15 detail: extra_query applied to key URI: update_url_query('https://example.com/key.bin', {'token': ['abc']}) \u2192 'https://example.com/key.bin?token=abc'. The key fetch uses `info_dict.get('_decryption_key_url') or decrypt_info['URI']` \u2192 the updated URI. So responses key must be the updated URL. Good.\n\nAlso in test 15, the fragment URL also gets extra query: 'https://example.com/seg0.ts?token=abc'. I could assert that too. Let me assert both.\n\n### Test 13: `requested == [MANIFEST_URL, 'https://example.com/key.bin']` \u2014 order: manifest first, then key during fragment processing. Good.\n\n### Now, is there any issue with `FakeResponse.read()` being called multiple times? Only once per response. Fine.\n\n### Potential issue: `monkeypatch.setattr(dl, 'report_warning', ...)` \u2014 dl.report_warning is used at line 72. Recorder appends args. Assertion: warnings[0][0] contains 'ffmpeg'. The message: 'hlsnative has detected features it does not support, extraction will be delegated to ffmpeg'. Good.\n\n### Test 2/3: errors[0][0] == 'pycrypto not found. Please install it.' \u2014 assert 'pycrypto' in it.\n\n### Let me now also handle: in test 3, info_dict has '_decryption_key_url': 'https://example.com/decryption-key'. can_download doesn't look at info_dict except is_live \u2192 manifest unsupported \u2192 False \u2192 line 69 True \u2192 error. Good.\n\n### Final check on `patch_fragment_methods` results repeat-last semantics: test 11 results [error, error] \u2014 two attempts, both raise. count: attempt1 count=0\u21921 (<=1 \u2192 report retry), attempt2 count=1\u21922 (>1 \u2192 no report). Then count(2) > retries(1) \u2192 skip disabled \u2192 report_error \u2192 return False. Downloads recorded: 2. Good.\n\nWait, actually let me re-trace: `while count <= fragment_retries:` with fragment_retries=1: count=0 \u2192 try \u2192 raise \u2192 count=1; `if count <= fragment_retries:` 1<=1 \u2192 report_retry. Loop: count=1 <= 1 \u2192 try \u2192 raise \u2192 count=2; 2<=1 False \u2192 no report. Loop condition: count=2 <= 1 False \u2192 exit. `if count > fragment_retries:` 2>1 \u2192 skip_unavailable_fragments False \u2192 report_error \u2192 return False. Good: 2 download attempts.\n\nTest 10: fragment_retries=1, skip=True. frag0: 2 attempts (both raise) \u2192 count=2 > 1 \u2192 skip \u2192 i+=1, media_sequence+=1, report_skip_fragment, continue. frag1: attempt count=0 \u2192 success \u2192 break. Good: 3 download calls total.\n\n### One more: `results` for test 10: [error, error, (True, b'frag1')] \u2014 indices 0,1 for frag0 attempts; index 2 for frag1. Good.\n\n### Now, `calls['download']` entries: {'url', 'headers'}. In test 10, headers for each: {} (no byte_range). Fine.\n\n### Also assert in test 10 that report_skip_fragment was called? I'd need to patch it. Optional \u2014 the append assertion already proves the skip happened. I'll patch report_skip_fragment to record and assert, for good measure. Actually, keep it simpler: assert via downloads/appends. Hmm, but asserting report_skip_fragment exercises... it's called at line 166 \u2014 already covered. I'll add the patch anyway for a stronger postcondition. Let me add skip recording in test 10:\n\n```python\n    skips = []\n    monkeypatch.setattr(dl, 'report_skip_fragment', lambda *a: skips.append(a))\n    ...\n    assert skips == [(1,)]\n```\n\nWait, report_skip_fragment(self, frag_index) \u2014 instance attr lambda *a: a=(1,). Good.\n\nSimilarly report_retry_fragment in test 10: retries recorded [(err, 1, 1, 1)]. Let me record count values: `retries.append((a[1], a[2]))` \u2192 [(1, 1)]. Eh, let me just record all args and assert length 1. Keep it simple: assert len(retries) == 1.\n\nHmm, actually the retry report happens once (count=1 attempt). Good.\n\n### Also in test 11, patch report_error and assert message contains 'giving up after 1 fragment retries'.\n\nMessage: 'giving up after %s fragment retries' % fragment_retries \u2192 'giving up after 1 fragment retries'. Assert 'giving up after 1 fragment retries' in errors[0][0].\n\n### Now finalize. Also, should I include a test for `is_live` \u2192 delegation? Not needed for 61-216 (line 68 branch already covered both ways).\n\nLet me also double check that in test 1, `dl._progress_hooks` \u2014 FileDownloader.__init__ added report_progress \u2192 len 1. The fake ffmpeg records hooks list \u2192 len 1. Assert equality of lengths. Good.\n\n### Write the file now.\n\n```python\n# -*- coding: utf-8 -*-\n\"\"\"Tests covering HlsFD.real_download (youtube_dl/downloader/hls.py, lines 61-216).\n\nAll network access and the FragmentFD bookkeeping machinery are replaced with\nrecording fakes (via ``monkeypatch``), so the tests are hermetic and leave no\nfiles or global state behind.\n\"\"\"\n\nimport binascii\n\nimport pytest\n\nfrom youtube_dl import YoutubeDL\nfrom youtube_dl.compat import compat_struct_pack, compat_urllib_error\nfrom youtube_dl.downloader import hls as hls_module\nfrom youtube_dl.downloader.hls import HlsFD\n\nMANIFEST_URL = 'https://example.com/video.m3u8'\n\n\nclass FakeResponse(object):\n    \"\"\"Minimal file-like object with geturl()/read(), like an urlopen result.\"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self, url, data):\n        self._url = url\n        self._data = data\n\n    def geturl(self):\n        return self._url\n\n    def read(self):\n        return self._data\n\n\ndef _as_string(url):\n    return url.get_full_url() if hasattr(url, 'get_full_url') else url\n\n\ndef make_downloader(monkeypatch, manifest, responses=None, params=None):\n    \"\"\"Create an HlsFD whose ydl.urlopen serves *manifest*/*responses*.\"\"\"\n    ydl = YoutubeDL(params if params is not None else {'quiet': True})\n    responses = dict(responses or {})\n    requested = []\n\n    def fake_urlopen(url):\n        url = _as_string(url)\n        requested.append(url)\n        result = responses.get(url, manifest)\n        if isinstance(result, Exception):\n            raise result\n        return FakeResponse(url, result)\n\n    monkeypatch.setattr(ydl, 'urlopen', fake_urlopen)\n    return HlsFD(ydl, ydl.params), requested\n\n\ndef patch_fragment_methods(monkeypatch, dl, results, fragment_index=0):\n    \"\"\"Replace FragmentFD's fragment machinery with recording fakes.\n\n    *results* is a list of ``(success, content)`` tuples or Exception\n    instances; the last entry is repeated once the list is exhausted.\n    \"\"\"\n    calls = {'prepare': [], 'download': [], 'append': [], 'finish': []}\n    state = {'next': 0}\n\n    def fake_prepare_and_start(ctx):\n        ctx['fragment_index'] = fragment_index\n        calls['prepare'].append(dict(ctx))\n\n    def fake_download(ctx, frag_url, info_dict, headers=None):\n        calls['download'].append({'url': frag_url, 'headers': dict(headers or {})})\n        index = state['next']\n        state['next'] += 1\n        result = results[index] if index < len(results) else results[-1]\n        if isinstance(result, Exception):\n            raise result\n        return result\n\n    def fake_append(ctx, frag_content):\n        calls['append'].append(frag_content)\n\n    def fake_finish(ctx):\n        calls['finish'].append(dict(ctx))\n\n    monkeypatch.setattr(dl, '_prepare_and_start_frag_download', fake_prepare_and_start)\n    monkeypatch.setattr(dl, '_download_fragment', fake_download)\n    monkeypatch.setattr(dl, '_append_fragment', fake_append)\n    monkeypatch.setattr(dl, '_finish_frag_download', fake_finish)\n    return calls\n\n\ndef patch_ffmpeg(monkeypatch):\n    \"\"\"Replace the FFmpegFD used for the fallback path with a recording fake.\"\"\"\n    calls = []\n\n    class FakeFFmpegFD(object):\n        def __init__(self, ydl, params):\n            self.ydl = ydl\n            self.params = params\n            self.hooks = []\n\n        def add_progress_hook(self, ph):\n            self.hooks.append(ph)\n\n        def real_download(self, filename, info_dict):\n            calls.append({\n                'filename': filename,\n                'info_dict': info_dict,\n                'hooks': list(self.hooks),\n            })\n            return True\n\n    monkeypatch.setattr(hls_module, 'FFmpegFD', FakeFFmpegFD)\n    return calls\n\n\ndef patch_aes(monkeypatch):\n    \"\"\"Replace the module level AES class with a recording fake.\"\"\"\n    calls = []\n\n    class FakeCipher(object):\n        def __init__(self, key, mode, iv):\n            self.key = key\n            self.mode = mode\n            self.iv = iv\n            calls.append(self)\n\n        def decrypt(self, data):\n            return b'decrypted:' + data\n\n    class FakeAES(object):\n        MODE_CBC = 'MODE_CBC'\n        new = staticmethod(lambda key, mode, iv: FakeCipher(key, mode, iv))\n\n    monkeypatch.setattr(hls_module, 'AES', FakeAES)\n    return calls\n```\n\nHmm, `new = staticmethod(lambda ...)` inside class body \u2014 works. Or define a static method properly. Let me write it properly:\n\n```python\n    class FakeAES(object):\n        MODE_CBC = 'MODE_CBC'\n\n        @staticmethod\n        def new(key, mode, iv):\n            return FakeCipher(key, mode, iv)\n```\n\nFine.\n\nNow the tests:\n\n```python\ndef test_delegates_to_ffmpeg_when_features_unsupported(monkeypatch):\n    manifest = '#EXTM3U\\n#EXT-X-MAP:URI=\"init.mp4\"\\n#EXTINF:10,\\nseg0.ts\\n'\n    dl, requested = make_downloader(monkeypatch, manifest)\n    warnings = []\n    monkeypatch.setattr(dl, 'report_warning', lambda *args: warnings.append(args))\n    ffmpeg_calls = patch_ffmpeg(monkeypatch)\n\n    result = dl.real_download('out.ts', {'url': MANIFEST_URL})\n\n    assert result is True\n    assert requested == [MANIFEST_URL]\n    assert len(warnings) == 1\n    assert 'delegated to ffmpeg' in warnings[0][0]\n    assert len(ffmpeg_calls) == 1\n    assert ffmpeg_calls[0]['filename'] == 'out.ts'\n    assert ffmpeg_calls[0]['info_dict']['url'] == MANIFEST_URL\n    assert len(ffmpeg_calls[0]['hooks']) == len(dl._progress_hooks)\n```\n\nWait \u2014 `lambda *args: warnings.append(args)` \u2014 report_warning called as self.report_warning(msg) \u2192 since instance attr, called with (msg,) \u2192 args=(msg,). Good.\n\n```python\ndef test_reports_pycrypto_error_for_extra_param_to_segment_url(monkeypatch):\n    manifest = '#EXTM3U\\n#EXT-X-MAP:URI=\"init.mp4\"\\n#EXTINF:10,\\nseg0.ts\\n'\n    dl, _ = make_downloader(monkeypatch, manifest)\n    errors = []\n    monkeypatch.setattr(dl, 'report_error', lambda *args: errors.append(args))\n    ffmpeg_calls = patch_ffmpeg(monkeypatch)\n\n    result = dl.real_download('out.ts', {\n        'url': MANIFEST_URL,\n        'extra_param_to_segment_url': 'token=abc',\n    })\n\n    assert result is False\n    assert len(errors) == 1\n    assert 'pycrypto not found' in errors[0][0]\n    assert ffmpeg_calls == []\n\n\ndef test_reports_pycrypto_error_for_decryption_key_url(monkeypatch):\n    manifest = '#EXTM3U\\n#EXT-X-MAP:URI=\"init.mp4\"\\n#EXTINF:10,\\nseg0.ts\\n'\n    dl, _ = make_downloader(monkeypatch, manifest)\n    errors = []\n    monkeypatch.setattr(dl, 'report_error', lambda *args: errors.append(args))\n    ffmpeg_calls = patch_ffmpeg(monkeypatch)\n\n    result = dl.real_download('out.ts', {\n        'url': MANIFEST_URL,\n        '_decryption_key_url': 'https://example.com/decryption.key',\n    })\n\n    assert result is False\n    assert len(errors) == 1\n    assert 'pycrypto not found' in errors[0][0]\n    assert ffmpeg_calls == []\n```\n\n```python\ndef test_basic_download_downloads_all_fragments(monkeypatch):\n    manifest = (\n        '#EXTM3U\\n'\n        '\\n'\n        '#EXT-X-KEY:METHOD=NONE\\n'\n        '#EXT-X-TARGETDURATION:10\\n'\n        '#EXTINF:10,\\n'\n        'seg0.ts\\n'\n        '#EXTINF:10,\\n'\n        'https://other.example.com/seg1.ts\\n'\n    )\n    dl, requested = make_downloader(monkeypatch, manifest)\n    calls = patch_fragment_methods(\n        monkeypatch, dl, [(True, b'frag0'), (True, b'frag1')])\n\n    result = dl.real_download('out.ts', {'url': MANIFEST_URL})\n\n    assert result is True\n    assert requested == [MANIFEST_URL]\n    assert calls['prepare'][0]['filename'] == 'out.ts'\n    assert calls['prepare'][0]['total_frags'] == 2\n    assert calls['prepare'][0]['ad_frags'] == 0\n    assert [download['url'] for download in calls['download']] == [\n        'https://example.com/seg0.ts',\n        'https://other.example.com/seg1.ts',\n    ]\n    assert all(download['headers'] == {} for download in calls['download'])\n    assert calls['append'] == [b'frag0', b'frag1']\n    assert len(calls['finish']) == 1\n```\n\n```python\ndef test_test_mode_downloads_only_first_fragment(monkeypatch):\n    manifest = '#EXTM3U\\n#EXTINF:10,\\nseg0.ts\\n#EXTINF:10,\\nseg1.ts\\n'\n    dl, _ = make_downloader(\n        monkeypatch, manifest, params={'quiet': True, 'test': True})\n    calls = patch_fragment_methods(monkeypatch, dl, [(True, b'frag0')])\n\n    result = dl.real_download('out.ts', {'url': MANIFEST_URL})\n\n    assert result is True\n    assert [download['url'] for download in calls['download']] == [\n        'https://example.com/seg0.ts']\n    assert calls['append'] == [b'frag0']\n    assert len(calls['finish']) == 1\n```\n\n```python\ndef test_resume_skips_already_downloaded_fragments(monkeypatch):\n    manifest = '#EXTM3U\\n#EXTINF:10,\\nseg0.ts\\n#EXTINF:10,\\nseg1.ts\\n'\n    dl, _ = make_downloader(monkeypatch, manifest)\n    calls = patch_fragment_methods(\n        monkeypatch, dl, [(True, b'frag1')], fragment_index=1)\n\n    result = dl.real_download('out.ts', {'url': MANIFEST_URL})\n\n    assert result is True\n    assert [download['url'] for download in calls['download']] == [\n        'https://example.com/seg1.ts']\n    assert calls['append'] == [b'frag1']\n```\n\n```python\ndef test_extra_param_to_segment_url_is_added_to_fragment_urls(monkeypatch):\n    manifest = '#EXTM3U\\n#EXTINF:10,\\nseg0.ts\\n'\n    dl, _ = make_downloader(monkeypatch, manifest)\n    calls = patch_fragment_methods(monkeypatch, dl, [(True, b'frag0')])\n\n    result = dl.real_download('out.ts', {\n        'url': MANIFEST_URL,\n        'extra_param_to_segment_url': 'token=abc',\n    })\n\n    assert result is True\n    assert calls['download'][0]['url'] == 'https://example.com/seg0.ts?token=abc'\n```\n\n```python\ndef test_ad_fragments_are_skipped(monkeypatch):\n    manifest = (\n        '#EXTM3U\\n'\n        '#ANVATO-SEGMENT-INFO:type=ad\\n'\n        'seg-ad0.ts\\n'\n        '#ANVATO-SEGMENT-INFO:type=master\\n'\n        'seg0.ts\\n'\n        '#UPLYNK-SEGMENT,ad\\n'\n        'seg-ad1.ts\\n'\n        '#UPLYNK-SEGMENT,segment\\n'\n        'seg1.ts\\n'\n    )\n    dl, _ = make_downloader(monkeypatch, manifest)\n    calls = patch_fragment_methods(\n        monkeypatch, dl, [(True, b'frag0'), (True, b'frag1')])\n\n    result = dl.real_download('out.ts', {'url': MANIFEST_URL})\n\n    assert result is True\n    assert calls['prepare'][0]['total_frags'] == 2\n    assert calls['prepare'][0]['ad_frags'] == 2\n    assert [download['url'] for download in calls['download']] == [\n        'https://example.com/seg0.ts',\n        'https://example.com/seg1.ts',\n    ]\n    assert calls['append'] == [b'frag0', b'frag1']\n```\n\n```python\ndef test_byterange_sets_range_headers(monkeypatch):\n    manifest = (\n        '#EXTM3U\\n'\n        '#EXT-X-BYTERANGE:1000@2000\\n'\n        'seg0.ts\\n'\n        '#EXT-X-BYTERANGE:500\\n'\n        'seg1.ts\\n'\n    )\n    dl, _ = make_downloader(monkeypatch, manifest)\n    calls = patch_fragment_methods(\n        monkeypatch, dl, [(True, b'frag0'), (True, b'frag1')])\n\n    result = dl.real_download('out.ts', {'url': MANIFEST_URL})\n\n    assert result is True\n    assert [download['headers'].get('Range') for download in calls['download']] == [\n        'bytes=2000-2999',\n        'bytes=3000-3499',\n    ]\n```\n\n```python\ndef test_http_error_retries_then_skips_fragment(monkeypatch):\n    manifest = '#EXTM3U\\n#EXTINF:10,\\nseg0.ts\\n#EXTINF:10,\\nseg1.ts\\n'\n    params = {\n        'quiet': True,\n        'fragment_retries': 1,\n        'skip_unavailable_fragments': True,\n    }\n    dl, _ = make_downloader(monkeypatch, manifest, params=params)\n    error = compat_urllib_error.HTTPError(\n        MANIFEST_URL, 503, 'Service Unavailable', {}, None)\n    retries = []\n    skips = []\n    monkeypatch.setattr(dl, 'report_retry_fragment', lambda *args: retries.append(args))\n    monkeypatch.setattr(dl, 'report_skip_fragment', lambda *args: skips.append(args))\n    calls = patch_fragment_methods(\n        monkeypatch, dl, [error, error, (True, b'frag1')])\n\n    result = dl.real_download('out.ts', {'url': MANIFEST_URL})\n\n    assert result is True\n    assert [download['url'] for download in calls['download']] == [\n        'https://example.com/seg0.ts',\n        'https://example.com/seg0.ts',\n        'https://example.com/seg1.ts',\n    ]\n    assert len(retries) == 1\n    assert skips == [(1,)]\n    assert calls['append'] == [b'frag1']\n    assert len(calls['finish']) == 1\n```\n\n```python\ndef test_http_error_gives_up_when_skipping_disabled(monkeypatch):\n    manifest = '#EXTM3U\\n#EXTINF:10,\\nseg0.ts\\n'\n    params = {\n        'quiet': True,\n        'fragment_retries': 1,\n        'skip_unavailable_fragments': False,\n    }\n    dl, _ = make_downloader(monkeypatch, manifest, params=params)\n    error = compat_urllib_error.HTTPError(MANIFEST_URL, 500, 'Server Error', {}, None)\n    errors = []\n    monkeypatch.setattr(dl, 'report_error', lambda *args: errors.append(args))\n    calls = patch_fragment_methods(monkeypatch, dl, [error, error])\n\n    result = dl.real_download('out.ts', {'url': MANIFEST_URL})\n\n    assert result is False\n    assert len(calls['download']) == 2\n    assert 'giving up after 1 fragment retries' in errors[0][0]\n    assert calls['append'] == []\n    assert calls['finish'] == []\n```\n\n```python\ndef test_fragment_download_failure_aborts(monkeypatch):\n    manifest = '#EXTM3U\\n#EXTINF:10,\\nseg0.ts\\n'\n    dl, _ = make_downloader(monkeypatch, manifest)\n    calls = patch_fragment_methods(monkeypatch, dl, [(False, None)])\n\n    result = dl.real_download('out.ts', {'url': MANIFEST_URL})\n\n    assert result is False\n    assert len(calls['download']) == 1\n    assert calls['append'] == []\n    assert calls['finish'] == []\n```\n\n```python\ndef test_aes128_decryption_with_explicit_iv(monkeypatch):\n    manifest = (\n        '#EXTM3U\\n'\n        '#EXT-X-KEY:METHOD=AES-128,'\n        'URI=\"https://example.com/key.bin\",'\n        'IV=0x1234567890abcdef1234567890abcdef\\n'\n        'seg0.ts\\n'\n    )\n    key = b'0123456789abcdef'\n    dl, requested = make_downloader(\n        monkeypatch, manifest, responses={'https://example.com/key.bin': key})\n    calls = patch_fragment_methods(monkeypatch, dl, [(True, b'\\x00' * 16)])\n    aes_calls = patch_aes(monkeypatch)\n\n    result = dl.real_download('out.ts', {'url': MANIFEST_URL})\n\n    assert result is True\n    assert requested == [MANIFEST_URL, 'https://example.com/key.bin']\n    assert len(aes_calls) == 1\n    assert aes_calls[0].key == key\n    assert aes_calls[0].iv == binascii.unhexlify('1234567890abcdef1234567890abcdef')\n    assert calls['append'] == [b'decrypted:' + b'\\x00' * 16]\n```\n\nWait \u2014 the manifest string concatenation: '#EXT-X-KEY:METHOD=AES-128,' 'URI=\"https://example.com/key.bin\",' 'IV=0x...\\n' \u2014 adjacent string literals concatenate. The full line: '#EXT-X-KEY:METHOD=AES-128,URI=\"https://example.com/key.bin\",IV=0x1234567890abcdef1234567890abcdef'. parse_m3u8_attributes regex: `(?P<key>[A-Z0-9-]+)=(?P<val>\"[^\"]+\"|[^\",]+)(?:,|$)`. For 'METHOD=AES-128,URI=\"https://example.com/key.bin\",IV=0x1234...': METHOD\u2192AES-128, URI\u2192\"https://example.com/key.bin\" (quoted, stripped), IV\u21920x1234... Good.\n\nHmm wait, one subtlety: the val regex `[^\",]+` for IV \u2014 '0x1234567890abcdef1234567890abcdef' then end \u2192 matches with $ . Good.\n\n```python\ndef test_aes128_default_iv_uses_media_sequence_and_relative_key_uri(monkeypatch):\n    manifest = (\n        '#EXTM3U\\n'\n        '#EXT-X-MEDIA-SEQUENCE:5\\n'\n        '#EXT-X-KEY:METHOD=AES-128,URI=\"key.bin\"\\n'\n        'seg0.ts\\n'\n    )\n    dl, requested = make_downloader(\n        monkeypatch, manifest, responses={'https://example.com/key.bin': b'K' * 16})\n    calls = patch_fragment_methods(monkeypatch, dl, [(True, b'\\x00' * 16)])\n    aes_calls = patch_aes(monkeypatch)\n\n    result = dl.real_download('out.ts', {'url': MANIFEST_URL})\n\n    assert result is True\n    assert 'https://example.com/key.bin' in requested\n    assert aes_calls[0].key == b'K' * 16\n    assert aes_calls[0].iv == compat_struct_pack('>8xq', 5)\n```\n\n```python\ndef test_aes128_key_uri_gets_extra_query(monkeypatch):\n    manifest = (\n        '#EXTM3U\\n'\n        '#EXT-X-KEY:METHOD=AES-128,URI=\"https://example.com/key.bin\"\\n'\n        'seg0.ts\\n'\n    )\n    dl, requested = make_downloader(\n        monkeypatch, manifest,\n        responses={'https://example.com/key.bin?token=abc': b'K' * 16})\n    calls = patch_fragment_methods(monkeypatch, dl, [(True, b'\\x00' * 16)])\n    patch_aes(monkeypatch)\n\n    result = dl.real_download('out.ts', {\n        'url': MANIFEST_URL,\n        'extra_param_to_segment_url': 'token=abc',\n    })\n\n    assert result is True\n    assert calls['download'][0]['url'] == 'https://example.com/seg0.ts?token=abc'\n    assert 'https://example.com/key.bin?token=abc' in requested\n```\n\n```python\ndef test_aes128_key_change_resets_cached_key(monkeypatch):\n    manifest = (\n        '#EXTM3U\\n'\n        '#EXT-X-KEY:METHOD=AES-128,URI=\"https://example.com/key1.bin\"\\n'\n        '#EXT-X-KEY:METHOD=AES-128,URI=\"https://example.com/key1.bin\"\\n'\n        'seg0.ts\\n'\n        '#EXT-X-KEY:METHOD=AES-128,URI=\"https://example.com/key2.bin\"\\n'\n        'seg1.ts\\n'\n    )\n    dl, requested = make_downloader(\n        monkeypatch, manifest,\n        responses={\n            'https://example.com/key1.bin': b'1' * 16,\n            'https://example.com/key2.bin': b'2' * 16,\n        })\n    calls = patch_fragment_methods(\n        monkeypatch, dl, [(True, b'\\x00' * 16), (True, b'\\x00' * 16)])\n    aes_calls = patch_aes(monkeypatch)\n\n    result = dl.real_download('out.ts', {'url': MANIFEST_URL})\n\n    assert result is True\n    assert [cipher.key for cipher in aes_calls] == [b'1' * 16, b'2' * 16]\n    assert requested.count('https://example.com/key1.bin') == 1\n    assert requested.count('https://example.com/key2.bin') == 1\n```\n\n```python\ndef test_aes128_key_is_cached_between_fragments(monkeypatch):\n    manifest = (\n        '#EXTM3U\\n'\n        '#EXT-X-KEY:METHOD=AES-128,URI=\"https://example.com/key.bin\"\\n'\n        'seg0.ts\\n'\n        'seg1.ts\\n'\n    )\n    dl, requested = make_downloader(\n        monkeypatch, manifest, responses={'https://example.com/key.bin': b'K' * 16})\n    calls = patch_fragment_methods(\n        monkeypatch, dl, [(True, b'\\x00' * 16), (True, b'\\x00' * 16)])\n    aes_calls = patch_aes(monkeypatch)\n\n    result = dl.real_download('out.ts', {'url': MANIFEST_URL})\n\n    assert result is True\n    assert requested.count('https://example.com/key.bin') == 1\n    assert len(aes_calls) == 2\n    assert all(cipher.key == b'K' * 16 for cipher in aes_calls)\n    assert calls['append'] == [b'decrypted:' + b'\\x00' * 16] * 2\n```\n\n```python\ndef test_aes128_skips_decryption_in_test_mode(monkeypatch):\n    manifest = (\n        '#EXTM3U\\n'\n        '#EXT-X-KEY:METHOD=AES-128,URI=\"https://example.com/key.bin\"\\n'\n        'seg0.ts\\n'\n    )\n    dl, _ = make_downloader(\n        monkeypatch, manifest,\n        responses={'https://example.com/key.bin': b'K' * 16},\n        params={'quiet': True, 'test': True})\n    calls = patch_fragment_methods(monkeypatch, dl, [(True, b'raw-frag')])\n    aes_calls = patch_aes(monkeypatch)\n\n    result = dl.real_download('out.ts', {'url': MANIFEST_URL})\n\n    assert result is True\n    assert aes_calls == []\n    assert calls['append'] == [b'raw-frag']\n    assert len(calls['finish']) == 1\n```\n\nNow \u2014 wait, in test_aes128_skips_decryption_in_test_mode, the key IS fetched (line 173-174 runs before the test check). requested includes key URL \u2014 provided in responses. Good.\n\nHmm, one thing to double check in test_basic: the manifest contains '#EXT-X-KEY:METHOD=NONE'. In the download loop, line 187: `elif line.startswith('#EXT-X-KEY'):` \u2192 decrypt_url = decrypt_info.get('URI') \u2192 None; decrypt_info = {'METHOD': 'NONE'}; line 190: 'NONE' != 'AES-128' \u2192 skip. Good. And subsequent fragments: decrypt_info['METHOD'] == 'AES-128' \u2192 False \u2192 no decryption. Good.\n\nNow \u2014 potential problem: `#EXT-X-KEY:METHOD=NONE` \u2014 can_download regex '#EXT-X-KEY:METHOD=(?!NONE|AES-128)' \u2014 no match. Good.\n\nAnother check \u2014 test_byterange: can_download \u2014 no KEY \u2192 is_aes128_enc False \u2192 checks pass. Good.\n\nNow, one more consideration on `patch_fragment_methods` \u2014 `results[-1]` when index >= len(results). For test_basic, results has exactly 2 entries and 2 downloads \u2192 fine. For test 10, 3 entries, 3 downloads \u2192 fine. For test 11, 2 entries, 2 downloads \u2192 fine. OK, but the repeat-last fallback is there for safety.\n\nWait, there's an issue with test 11: results [error, error] \u2014 index 0 \u2192 error (raise), index 1 \u2192 error (raise). Good.\n\nNow \u2014 `compat_urllib_error.HTTPError(MANIFEST_URL, 503, 'Service Unavailable', {}, None)` \u2014 in Python 3, HTTPError.__init__ with fp=None: \n\n```python\nclass HTTPError(URLError, urllib.response.addinfourl):\n    def __init__(self, url, code, msg, hdrs, fp):\n        self.code = code\n        self.msg = msg\n        self.hdrs = hdrs\n        self.fp = fp\n        self.filename = url\n        # The addinfourl that we've inherited from doesn't have a\n        # __init__ that takes the parameters we need...\n        if fp is not None:\n            self._method = None  # ?\n```\n\nHmm, actually current CPython:\n\n```python\n    def __init__(self, url, code, msg, hdrs, fp):\n        self.code = code\n        self.msg = msg\n        self.hdrs = hdrs\n        self.fp = fp\n        self.filename = url\n        if fp is None:\n            self._orig_fp = None\n        ...\n```\n\nI'm fairly confident `HTTPError(url, code, msg, {}, None)` works \u2014 it's used widely in tests. error_to_compat_str(err) \u2192 str(err) \u2192 'HTTP Error 503: Service Unavailable'. Good.\n\nHmm, wait \u2014 error_to_compat_str: \n\n```python\ndef error_to_compat_str(exception):\n    error_str = str(exception)\n    ...\n    return error_str\n```\n\nFine.\n\nAnd `format_retries(1)` \u2192 '1'. Fine.\n\nNow \u2014 one more thought about `YoutubeDL({'quiet': True})`: YoutubeDL.__init__ might require 'logger' handling etc. It's fine. But \u2014 hmm, does YoutubeDL.__init__ possibly call `self._setup_opener()` which creates a urllib opener \u2014 no network. Fine.\n\nActually, wait. There's one more potential gotcha: YoutubeDL.__init__ in youtube-dl does:\n\n```python\n        self.params['outtmpl'] = ...\n```\n\nNo... it does things like:\n\n```python\n        if params.get('bidi_workaround')...\n```\n\nNothing problematic with {'quiet': True}.\n\nHmm, but actually \u2014 I realize there might be an issue with `YoutubeDL.to_screen` when 'quiet' is True: it returns without printing. Good.\n\nBut `report_warning` \u2192 `self.ydl.report_warning(message)` \u2192 YoutubeDL.report_warning \u2192 `self.report_warning(message)`... In the delegation test I patch dl.report_warning (the downloader's), so ydl's isn't called. Good.\n\nIn tests where I don't patch report_warning/report_error but they might be called: \n- test_basic etc.: no warnings/errors expected. Actually wait \u2014 does anything call report_warning in the happy path? No.\n- test 10 (retry/skip): report_retry_fragment and report_skip_fragment are patched on dl. But wait \u2014 I patch `dl.report_retry_fragment` \u2014 the code calls `self.report_retry_fragment(err, frag_index, count, fragment_retries)` \u2192 instance attr \u2192 recorder. Good. report_skip_fragment similarly.\n\nHmm, but hold on: FragmentFD.report_retry_fragment is defined on FragmentFD (per get_info). The code calls self.report_retry_fragment \u2014 instance attribute patch works.\n\nOK. Now \u2014 one more subtle thing: in `make_downloader`, `HlsFD(ydl, ydl.params)` \u2014 FileDownloader.__init__ does `self.add_progress_hook(self.report_progress)`. report_progress is a bound method; fine.\n\nNow let me reconsider the `test` param propagation: `self.params.get('test', False)` \u2014 params is the dict I passed. Good.\n\nAlso `fragment_retries` default 0: in tests without it, `while count <= 0:` \u2192 one attempt; on HTTPError \u2192 count=1; `if count <= 0` False; loop exits; count(1) > 0 \u2192 skip (default skip_unavailable_fragments True) \u2192 skip. Not tested but fine.\n\nNow \u2014 is there any issue with `calls['prepare'][0]['filename']`? ctx includes 'filename': filename \u2192 'out.ts'. Good.\n\nLet me also double-check `update_url_query` behavior for 'https://example.com/seg0.ts' with {'token': ['abc']}:\n\n```python\ndef update_url_query(url, query):\n    ...\n    parsed_url = compat_urlparse.urlparse(url)\n    ...\n    return compat_url